WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.560
Carthage, North Africa, the year 197.

2
00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:07.630
A brilliant writer takes
on the Roman governors.

3
00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:11.460
He mocks their unjust trials,
answers every slander,

4
00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:16.260
and coins a famous line: the
blood of Christians is seed.

5
00:00:16.310 --> 00:00:22.010
He fights false teachers too, and gives
Latin theology a new word: Trinitas.

6
00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:26.250
Yet later, he calls most of his
fellow Christians unspiritual.

7
00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:31.530
So why did the sharpest early defender
of the church turn on so many Christians?

8
00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:35.130
In this mission, you'll sort
his writings onto three shelves:

9
00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:38.000
defending, teaching and conduct.

10
00:00:38.050 --> 00:00:42.650
Then you'll weigh a long debate:
did he ever really leave the church?

11
00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:47.640
Your mission: find out why the church's
sharpest defender ended up calling most

12
00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:49.300
Christians unspiritual.
